begin model
#@model_id: m09_preequilibration
#@title: Pre-equilibration relaxation (PyBNF new-era pre-equilibration recovery fixture)
#@description: Birth-death with a SWITCHABLE production. 0 -> A at rate k_prod*Production_isOn,
#  A -> 0 at rate k_deg. Equilibrating with Production_isOn=1 settles A to its steady state
#  A_ss = k_prod/k_deg; switching production OFF (Production_isOn=0) then makes A decay as
#  A(t) = (k_prod/k_deg)*exp(-k_deg*t). The measurement's t=0 value is ENTIRELY the equilibration
#  steady state, so a correct fit must carry state across the two phases (ADR-0052 #440): if
#  carry-over broke, the measurement would start at the seed A=0 and stay flat, matching nothing.
#
# New-era conventions (see tests/test_recovery.py):
#   * NO `begin actions` block: PyBNF synthesizes the two-phase protocol (equilibrate to steady
#     state -> setParameter -> measure) from the experiment:'s `preequilibrate:`/`condition:` +
#     the data grid -- there is no hand-written action.
#   * Free parameters bind BY ID (ADR-0034, edition >= 2): the fitted `k_deg` is a bare
#     model-parameter id (no `__FREE` marker); the optimizer overrides it in place.
#   * `Production_isOn` is a 0/1 flag the two conditions set via inline setParameter; `k_prod`
#     is a fixed (known) production rate.

begin parameters
  k_prod           3.0    # production rate (fixed/known)
  k_deg            2.0    # degradation rate (the FITTED free parameter, bound by id)
  Production_isOn  1      # 0/1 flag: the conditions set this inline (equilibrate ON, measure OFF)
end parameters

begin molecule types
  A()
end molecule types

begin seed species
  A()  0
end seed species

begin observables
  Molecules  A_tot  A()
end observables

begin functions
  # production is gated by the flag: full rate when ON, zero when OFF (the receptor
  # func()*Ligand_isPresent idiom that makes a mid-protocol setParameter switch a reaction)
  prod_rate()  k_prod * Production_isOn
end functions

begin reaction rules
  birth: 0 -> A()    prod_rate()
  death: A() -> 0    k_deg
end reaction rules

end model
